.TH EZCON 1 "2026-09-20" "caveutils" "caveutils Manual"
.SH NAME
ezcon \- terminal manager for containers, images, volumes and
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ezcon -e ENGINE
.br
.B ezcon VIEW
.br
.B ezcon ENTER
.br
.B ezcon ALT-1..5
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ezcon
.nf
networks, built on lib/lazytui.sh. One tool for both Docker and Podman
(pods too); it wraps the real binary, found in PATH skipping this script,
so it never calls itself.

  ezcon [-e docker|podman|both|qemu] [containers|images|volumes|networks|pods|vms]

Docker and Podman show up TOGETHER when both are installed: one list,
each row tagged with its engine, and every action goes to the row's own
engine (marked rows may even mix both). Tab cycles both -> docker ->
podman. -e (or EZCON_ENGINES) sets where it starts, e.g. `ezcon -e podman`.
Creating something (run, pull, create) asks which engine when both are in
use; prune and system prune run on every engine in use. Arrows or Tab move, space marks rows like nnn, / searches,
and every action runs on all marked rows (or the current one). The list
refreshes by itself every REFRESH_MS milliseconds (top of the script, or
LAZYCTL_REFRESH; 0 turns it off). Alt-1..5 switch views. The key bar
shows every key of the current view.

Containers: logs (Enter), follow logs, shell, start, stop, restart,
  kill, pause, unpause, remove, inspect, stats, run a new one, prune.
Images: run, pull again (update), remove, history, inspect, search the
  registry and pull, prune dangling.
Volumes and networks: create, remove, inspect, prune.
Pods (podman): start, stop, restart, remove, create, inspect.
VMs (qemu, Alt-6 or `ezcon -e qemu`): every disk image in VM_IMAGES is a
  VM, with a NAME.conf in VM_CONF for its settings (RAM, CPUs, ISO, UEFI,
  display, ssh port, ...) - existing images work with the defaults. Start
  (headless or a window), ACPI shutdown, kill, reset, pause, ssh into the
  guest through a forwarded port, serial console, new VM wizard, attach an
  installer ISO, edit the config, disk snapshots (create, revert, drop),
  delete. Needs qemu and qemu-img; socat for shutdown, reset, pause and
  the serial console.

Destructive actions (kill, remove, prune) ask first. When an action
fails its output is kept on screen until you press Enter.

.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -e ENGINE
docker or podman (default: docker if installed, else podman)
.TP
.B VIEW
start in this view (default containers)
.TP
.B ENTER
container logs / image run / inspect
.TP
.B ALT-1..5
switch view
